WEBVTT

01:50.360 --> 01:52.779
Noble Elder, are you awake?

01:53.988 --> 01:55.281
Yes.

02:04.958 --> 02:06.292
Good morning.

02:06.376 --> 02:08.378
Sorry about this.

02:11.381 --> 02:13.007
You look very tired.

02:13.716 --> 02:15.802
You should rest here for a while.

02:16.553 --> 02:18.930
CENTER BOXING GYM
NEW STUDENTS WELCOME

02:23.518 --> 02:27.689
<i>Akio Mani, the Oriental and Pacific
super welterweight champion.</i>

02:27.772 --> 02:31.609
Lastly, you've never lost
in your amateur and pro careers.

02:31.693 --> 02:35.446
What's more, all 14 of your pro fights
ended in first-round KO victories.

02:36.197 --> 02:39.701
The number of matches and rounds fought
in your career are the same.

02:39.784 --> 02:41.452
Did you plan for that?

02:42.036 --> 02:44.706
I'm not keeping track of the numbers.

02:45.540 --> 02:50.211
What I focus on is where
the extraordinary happens, the ring.

02:50.295 --> 02:53.339
I don't want to waste
any time in that space.

02:54.924 --> 02:58.595
In response to my opponent's action,
I make the most logical reaction.

02:59.179 --> 03:02.599
Anything longer than three minutes
makes no sense.

03:03.183 --> 03:06.603
Does that mean that you'll also end
the next world title match in one round?

03:07.270 --> 03:09.355
I will do what's logical.

03:12.233 --> 03:13.568
Thank you.

03:13.651 --> 03:16.613
- Thank you, Chairman.
- I look forward to the title match.

03:18.156 --> 03:19.616
What a lot of commotion.

03:31.628 --> 03:32.462
What's that?

03:36.466 --> 03:38.384
Well, that was...

03:41.638 --> 03:42.805
Impossible.

03:42.889 --> 03:45.516
He destroyed a heavy punching bag
with a bare-fisted straight right?

03:45.600 --> 03:46.893
That makes no sense.

03:47.560 --> 03:49.896
Well, yeah, it sure doesn't.

03:50.521 --> 03:51.397
Is he here?

03:51.481 --> 03:53.650
Yeah, he's facing the mirror.

04:05.370 --> 04:06.913
Can I spar with him?

04:06.996 --> 04:08.915
What? With him?!

04:09.499 --> 04:11.417
He can do it.

04:13.169 --> 04:14.629
I won't hurt him.

04:16.005 --> 04:16.923
Yes?

04:17.006 --> 04:19.926
I think this is a really rare chance, but...

04:20.009 --> 04:21.761
I don't mind in the least.

04:22.845 --> 04:24.430
So, who's it with?

04:24.514 --> 04:27.433
Hi! With me. <i>Xièxie!</i>

04:30.853 --> 04:32.188
I refuse.

04:34.023 --> 04:36.943
Refuse? Are you...

04:37.026 --> 04:39.862
I'd have too much
of an advantage against him.

04:40.446 --> 04:44.450
At his strength level, I wouldn't be able
to use all my strength against him.

04:47.537 --> 04:50.456
Not with him! It's too dangerous.

04:52.875 --> 04:54.961
You must not underestimate martial arts.

04:55.920 --> 04:57.547
Somebody put gloves on him.

04:58.047 --> 04:59.549
You're in for it now.

04:59.632 --> 05:01.592
There's no stopping it now.

05:01.676 --> 05:04.679
It goes without saying,
but boxing and kung fu are different.

05:04.762 --> 05:06.973
You're the one doing the underestimating!

05:07.557 --> 05:10.476
Hey, Mr. Kung Fu, you can kick too.

05:11.811 --> 05:14.188
You can kick, right?

05:14.272 --> 05:15.732
Hey, Mani!

05:24.073 --> 05:26.492
Don't you want to box?

05:28.328 --> 05:31.497
Naturally, I don't plan on kicking.
There's no need to kick.

05:32.081 --> 05:35.001
Even so, I'm telling you
that it'll be dangerous for you.

05:36.586 --> 05:38.504
Uh-oh...

05:39.130 --> 05:40.506
What's wrong with you guys?

05:41.257 --> 05:45.762
Since you ain't gettin' him ready,
he keeps yammerin' on!

05:47.638 --> 05:52.268
Coach, a minute ago, you said
that boxing and kung fu are different.

05:53.186 --> 05:54.354
You are wrong.

05:55.355 --> 05:58.524
As boxing uses fists to fight,
it can be considered kung fu.

05:59.275 --> 06:00.526
Unperfected, at that.

06:02.612 --> 06:03.780
I will now show you...

06:05.740 --> 06:07.283
the basis for this.

06:08.034 --> 06:09.285
Begin!

06:11.454 --> 06:14.040
<i>There is the phrase
"to be in one's element."</i>

06:14.749 --> 06:19.587
<i>The coach, Genichi Fukamachi,
age 46, would later say this.</i>

06:20.171 --> 06:21.798
<i>"I had a bad feeling."</i>

06:22.965 --> 06:25.301
<i>"His stance showed he was in his element."</i>

06:49.409 --> 06:50.326
Holy...

06:51.911 --> 06:54.539
Whoa! He's been knocked out cold.

06:55.164 --> 06:56.916
He hit his head.

07:02.547 --> 07:03.631
A right, huh?

07:04.841 --> 07:06.008
I didn't even see it.

07:15.560 --> 07:16.477
Hey.

07:18.563 --> 07:19.480
What are you doing?

07:20.606 --> 07:21.441
Training.

07:22.066 --> 07:24.735
What kind of training? Huh?

07:26.320 --> 07:28.990
Didn't you come here to learn boxing?

07:29.699 --> 07:30.533
That's right.

07:30.616 --> 07:32.994
Then you'd better do some boxing.

07:33.077 --> 07:36.998
Jumping rope, shadow boxing,
the sandbag, the speed ball.

07:37.623 --> 07:39.750
Aren't you gonna do any proper boxing?!

07:41.961 --> 07:47.258
Then how come I was able to knock down
someone who did proper boxing?

07:49.510 --> 07:52.763
There's no better way to justify
your own opinion than through fighting.

07:52.847 --> 07:56.517
If you believe that you are correct,
then I would like you to show me

07:57.101 --> 08:00.897
a powerful boxer who is no match
for my martial arts.

08:02.231 --> 08:04.192
If I am knocked down,

08:04.734 --> 08:08.613
I'll jump rope, shadowbox, punch the ball,
even stand on my head or dance.

08:09.280 --> 08:10.656
Whatever you tell me to do.

08:13.743 --> 08:15.578
Your logic is faultless.

08:16.370 --> 08:19.957
You don't win because you're correct.
You're correct because you win.

08:20.750 --> 08:23.586
Coach, we're the losers here.

08:24.253 --> 08:25.379
At least for today.

08:26.672 --> 08:28.674
But I'm sure you understand this, pal.

08:29.467 --> 08:32.428
You've turned all the boxers
in the world against you.

08:36.641 --> 08:39.560
SHINSHINKAI HEADQUARTERS
THE WAY OF KARATE

08:55.535 --> 08:58.287
<i>Don't think about having lost it.</i>

09:01.666 --> 09:03.000
<i>You haven't lost it.</i>

09:05.127 --> 09:06.087
<i>You've obtained it.</i>

09:07.046 --> 09:09.924
<i>What? What have I obtained?</i>

09:11.259 --> 09:12.093
<i>Being one-armed...</i>

09:13.302 --> 09:15.596
<i>My own original one-armed style!</i>

09:30.778 --> 09:32.363
Baki...

09:36.701 --> 09:41.998
Since the doors are closed,
I guess you trespassed through a window.

09:42.915 --> 09:47.003
It sure wasn't easy
climbing up to the ninth floor.

09:47.086 --> 09:49.255
You really are something, Baki Hanma.

09:49.964 --> 09:51.882
So, what brings you here today?

09:52.592 --> 09:54.176
You're amazing, Katsumi.

09:54.927 --> 09:57.096
It hasn't been long
since you lost your arm,

09:57.179 --> 09:59.640
but you're already mastering a new style.

10:00.224 --> 10:01.892
Does it appear that way?

10:03.978 --> 10:06.022
Though it isn't easy,

10:06.772 --> 10:11.152
instead of thinking about what I've lost,
I work to think about what I've gained.

10:11.819 --> 10:13.154
<i>In sword fighting,</i>

10:13.237 --> 10:16.157
<i>they strive to master
the use of a single sword.</i>

10:16.866 --> 10:20.411
<i>That skill is most definitely not inferior
to the two-sword method.</i>

10:20.995 --> 10:23.247
There are plenty of clear precedents.

10:23.748 --> 10:25.499
I was fortunate.

10:26.125 --> 10:30.921
There must be something I can obtain
by being placed in this situation.

10:32.256 --> 10:33.132
Right?

10:34.717 --> 10:36.677
You really are incredible, Katsumi.

10:37.511 --> 10:40.931
When your dad's a big-shot,
it's tough being the son.

10:41.599 --> 10:45.186
The greatest father-son fight
in the history of the world.

10:46.687 --> 10:48.189
They're exaggerating.

10:48.272 --> 10:50.316
It can't be helped.

10:50.399 --> 10:54.528
Yujiro Hanma versus
Baki Hanma is currently...

10:56.781 --> 10:59.450
the greatest matchup conceivable.

11:02.036 --> 11:04.955
I don't even hate him anymore.

11:05.623 --> 11:07.458
But I've still decided to fight him.

11:10.336 --> 11:11.253
I wonder why.

11:12.546 --> 11:13.923
Do you need a reason?

11:15.049 --> 11:16.217
No.

11:17.009 --> 11:19.220
Even if I did, there's no stopping it.

11:21.681 --> 11:23.224
Because we're father and son.

11:23.933 --> 11:25.476
Isn't that enough?

11:28.646 --> 11:29.480
Amazing.

11:35.069 --> 11:37.488
Because you are father and son.

11:40.950 --> 11:41.909
That's good enough.

11:51.085 --> 11:53.879
It's spread everywhere.

11:57.383 --> 12:00.052
What? Boxing?

12:00.136 --> 12:02.304
That's right. Boxing.

12:02.888 --> 12:03.806
But why?

12:03.889 --> 12:07.810
Sea King Retsu has even obtained
the title of "Sea King" in kung fu,

12:08.477 --> 12:09.603
so why become a boxer?

12:10.104 --> 12:11.522
Not a boxer.

12:15.276 --> 12:18.195
Sea King Retsu will remain Sea King Retsu

12:18.279 --> 12:20.823
and get in the ring
fighting Sea King Retsu-style.

12:22.408 --> 12:23.325
Then...

12:23.409 --> 12:25.828
He won't use boxing techniques.

12:25.911 --> 12:28.330
He'll climb his way up
using only kung fu skills.

12:30.958 --> 12:32.835
Will it really be so easy?

12:37.047 --> 12:38.424
Of course it won't be easy.

12:39.675 --> 12:42.386
No matter how you look at it,
it won't be easy.

12:43.012 --> 12:44.805
"Punch without getting punched."

12:44.889 --> 12:48.434
The simple game has been in existence
for over 150 years.

12:49.560 --> 12:52.354
<i>Kung fu has a 4,000-year history.</i>

12:52.438 --> 12:54.732
<i>There's no need to mention
its value or influence.</i>

12:55.232 --> 12:58.110
<i>Boxing is considered a modern sport.</i>

12:58.194 --> 13:01.822
<i>Though it has only a 150-year history,
there's nothing slack about it.</i>

13:02.323 --> 13:06.994
<i>Objectively, its speedy development
cannot be compared to that of kung fu.</i>

13:07.077 --> 13:09.497
Western kung fu
shouldn't be underestimated.

13:11.582 --> 13:14.001
It will test the present Sea King Retsu.

13:14.084 --> 13:16.003
And his future.

13:19.590 --> 13:21.509
What is Retsu's weight?

13:22.092 --> 13:23.511
One hundred and six kilos.

13:23.594 --> 13:26.514
Aw, man. How far will he go?

13:27.139 --> 13:28.766
Naturally, until he loses.

13:29.642 --> 13:31.769
Well, those are his own words.

13:33.854 --> 13:34.980
SHINSHINKAI HEADQUARTERS

13:35.064 --> 13:36.023
He's an idiot.

13:38.943 --> 13:41.403
CENTER BOXING GYM
NEW STUDENTS WELCOME

13:51.622 --> 13:52.748
Retsu.

13:52.832 --> 13:53.666
Yes?

13:54.250 --> 13:55.668
Put on gloves.

13:57.169 --> 13:59.421
You'll be sparring.
Hurry up and get 'em on.

13:59.505 --> 14:00.756
With who?

14:01.507 --> 14:06.428
You're just a student here,
so just do as you're told!

14:08.013 --> 14:09.265
All right.

14:11.517 --> 14:15.145
I didn't want to get rough

14:15.229 --> 14:17.815
but I've gotta show you
that we mean business too.

14:18.399 --> 14:20.568
This is probably what you wanted.

14:20.651 --> 14:25.114
An opponent you can fight with your all,
but who won't succumb to your skills.

14:25.197 --> 14:27.825
An honest-to-goodness heavyweight.

14:27.908 --> 14:30.327
He was in the military
until three years ago.

14:30.995 --> 14:33.330
He'd come from base to practice here.

14:33.414 --> 14:36.333
Since he's so big,
he couldn't debut in Japan.

14:36.917 --> 14:38.836
But he debuted back home after discharge.

14:39.420 --> 14:41.255
He's nine for nine with eight KOs.

14:41.338 --> 14:44.341
He knocked out all of his opponents
except in his debut match.

14:44.425 --> 14:48.095
He came back here to his old haunt
the day before yesterday to get ready.

14:48.178 --> 14:49.722
As you can see,

14:49.805 --> 14:53.100
in weight, career and technique, in fact,

14:53.183 --> 14:55.436
in every way he surpasses you!

14:55.519 --> 14:58.230
Take this opportunity
to learn what boxing is really about!

15:00.316 --> 15:02.109
I don't need any headgear.

15:02.651 --> 15:04.486
I figured you'd say that.

15:05.279 --> 15:07.740
But I sure ain't lettin' anyone
die at my gym.

15:10.242 --> 15:11.243
Don't die out there.

15:17.249 --> 15:18.250
<i>I see.</i>

15:18.876 --> 15:22.504
<i>I see, I see.
He truly does have great talent.</i>

15:22.588 --> 15:25.257
<i>His massive frame is far larger than mine.</i>

15:25.341 --> 15:28.135
<i>By ten kilos... No, by at least 15 kilos.</i>

15:28.969 --> 15:32.640
<i>Even so, his footwork is smooth,
deceptive given his great size.</i>

15:33.223 --> 15:34.892
<i>He's got a long reach as well.</i>

15:40.439 --> 15:41.398
Amazing.

15:50.532 --> 15:51.408
<i>I see.</i>

15:52.534 --> 15:53.994
<i>I see, I see.</i>

15:54.995 --> 15:56.664
<i>His speed, excellent.</i>

15:57.247 --> 15:58.916
<i>His power, excellent.</i>

16:02.002 --> 16:04.421
<i>His grip, weak.</i>

16:05.130 --> 16:08.175
<i>Combat sports are not based
on street fighting.</i>

16:08.968 --> 16:11.387
<i>As long as rules dictate
the use of gloves,</i>

16:11.470 --> 16:14.807
<i>it is inevitable that the properties
of the glove become used as weapons.</i>

16:15.432 --> 16:20.312
<i>Hence, compared to barehanded karate
and kung fu, the grip is weaker.</i>

16:21.355 --> 16:23.357
<i>Sea King Retsu, who lives by martial arts,</i>

16:23.440 --> 16:26.443
<i>perceived his opponents weak grip,
just by the feel of his punch.</i>

16:27.611 --> 16:28.445
<i>The reach...</i>

16:40.249 --> 16:44.044
<i>The thickest and strongest bone
in the human body is the frontal skull.</i>

16:44.545 --> 16:48.841
<i>A clenched fist consists
of 27 large and small slivers of bone.</i>

16:49.425 --> 16:51.844
<i>Because the fist
had not been specifically trained,</i>

16:51.927 --> 16:54.221
<i>its destruction was completely inevitable.</i>

16:57.850 --> 16:58.726
I see.

17:00.686 --> 17:02.813
So, what did Baki have to say?

17:06.942 --> 17:08.986
He wants to meet you.

17:13.115 --> 17:14.241
Meet me for what?

17:16.493 --> 17:18.037
Baki has changed.

17:19.705 --> 17:21.999
Incredibly, with you, he wants to...

17:28.589 --> 17:31.759
That bastard!
How dare he say such a thing!

17:35.345 --> 17:37.514
<i>It broke... completely!</i>

17:38.849 --> 17:40.517
<i>Does he plan on continuing?</i>

17:44.563 --> 17:45.522
<i>It's time to...</i>

17:46.607 --> 17:49.276
<i>What the heck is he gonna do
from that stance?!</i>

17:49.359 --> 17:50.360
Three.

17:51.862 --> 17:52.905
Two.

17:54.823 --> 17:56.033
<i>He was aiming at...</i>

17:57.367 --> 17:58.285
One.

17:58.994 --> 18:03.540
<i>...not his weak point,
but the humerus he was using to block.</i>

18:05.000 --> 18:07.544
<i>The legend of the boxer Sea King Retsu</i>

18:08.462 --> 18:10.089
<i>had only just begun.</i>

18:12.883 --> 18:15.803
Did that really come out
of that bastard's mouth?!

18:17.387 --> 18:18.847
Just calm down, Ogre.

18:18.931 --> 18:21.308
You're frightening off the waitstaff.

18:25.479 --> 18:26.313
Strydum.

18:27.189 --> 18:28.816
Give me the details.

18:29.983 --> 18:31.860
It surprised me too.

18:31.944 --> 18:34.154
It was a real bolt out of the blue.

18:39.034 --> 18:40.702
What the hell?!

18:41.286 --> 18:42.704
What did you just say?

18:43.372 --> 18:44.456
You heard me.

18:45.165 --> 18:47.960
Do you have any idea what you're saying?!

18:49.044 --> 18:50.087
That's abnormal.

18:51.088 --> 18:53.799
You doubt what you just heard me say.

18:53.882 --> 18:55.717
Your reaction is far more abnormal.

18:59.304 --> 19:00.722
Yeah, but...

19:00.806 --> 19:03.475
What's so crazy about what I said?

19:04.059 --> 19:06.645
I want to have a leisurely meal
with my father.

19:06.728 --> 19:08.480
What's so crazy about that?

19:09.064 --> 19:12.484
As his son, I want to eat with him.
That's perfectly normal!

19:13.652 --> 19:14.987
You're exactly right.

19:15.070 --> 19:16.113
Then...

19:16.196 --> 19:17.322
Baki.

19:18.657 --> 19:20.242
Don't act dumb!

19:20.993 --> 19:24.997
You know perfectly well
that what you're saying is outrageous.

19:25.664 --> 19:30.210
The abnormality of Baki Hanma
and Yujiro Hanma sharing a table...

19:31.378 --> 19:33.255
Just imagine it!

19:34.423 --> 19:36.258
<i>The unnaturalness of it!</i>

19:47.102 --> 19:53.275
To cook rice, heat up miso soup,
smack our lips at the frugal food,

19:54.026 --> 19:56.528
and share the blessing
of being able to eat.

19:56.612 --> 19:58.989
Oh, dessert would be nice too.

19:59.615 --> 20:01.533
The latest ice cream bar.

20:02.117 --> 20:04.953
We'd say, "Just look at what
they've come up with now."

20:05.621 --> 20:10.042
You know, it sometimes happens,
when we talk about everyday things.

20:10.834 --> 20:14.546
Two people of different generations clash
over a difference of opinion.

20:15.464 --> 20:18.050
When that happens,
Dad would be really stubborn.

20:19.134 --> 20:21.553
"You moron! You make me sick!"

20:22.221 --> 20:25.557
"I'll knock your block off
and fix your sissy way of thinking!"

20:26.558 --> 20:28.310
He'd be against it from the start.

20:28.810 --> 20:31.063
Then I wouldn't give any ground either.

20:31.647 --> 20:33.357
"You're always like that, Dad!"

20:33.440 --> 20:35.984
"You won't listen to other opinions!"

20:36.068 --> 20:37.069
Baki...

20:37.152 --> 20:39.071
"You're so narrow-minded!"

20:39.154 --> 20:40.072
Baki!

20:40.155 --> 20:43.659
"Don't you dare get smart with me,
you punk! Shut your trap!"

20:43.742 --> 20:44.576
Baki!

20:53.919 --> 20:59.049
Do you really think
that kind of Yujiro Hanma exists?

20:59.132 --> 21:02.386
The sort of bickering
that's normal in most households...

21:02.469 --> 21:05.347
You may want to enjoy that ordinary stuff.

21:07.683 --> 21:10.602
But you and your father
have grown too big for that!

21:17.943 --> 21:21.363
And how come I'm always...

21:24.449 --> 21:27.119
the one who has to cook the rice?

21:32.207 --> 21:36.878
Dad's got to step up
and cook rice sometimes.

21:41.925 --> 21:44.636
You can never tell
what might happen in this world.

21:45.387 --> 21:47.514
But that won't ever happen!

21:57.065 --> 21:58.775
Me...

21:59.401 --> 22:01.528
Cook rice?!

22:17.502 --> 22:19.671
<i>Cook rice, huh?</i>
